{:edb/db-before-t 2781 :edb/db-after-t 2782 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536094 50 #inst "2026-10-09T14:50:57.160Z" 13194139536094 true] [17592186078407 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383286 13194139536094 true] [17592186078407 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383293 13194139536094 true] [17592186078407 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383303 13194139536094 true] [17592186078407 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383306 13194139536094 true] [17592186078490 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383279 13194139536094 true] [17592186078490 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383296 13194139536094 true] [17592186078490 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383300 13194139536094 true] [17592186078851 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536094 true] [17592186078851 1100 "${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{x}{7\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=$" 13194139536094 true] [17592186078851 1100 "What is $lim_(x → 0)\\frac{x}{7\\sin x}$?" 13194139536094 false] [17592186078851 1145 "Notice that as $x\\to 0,$ both numerator and denominator approach $0.$\n\nSo, if we attempt to evaluate the limit directly, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{x}{7\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=\\frac{0}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is an indeterminate form.\n\nInstead, let's recall the following special limit:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}=1\n$$\n\nRewriting the given limit using the algebra of limits and applying our special limit, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{x}{7\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}(\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot \\frac{x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to 0}{(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x})}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot {[{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot {1}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383279 1017 #edb/ref 17592186383280 13194139536094 true] [17592186383279 1089 "q-105409" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383279 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13