83282 1034 "\\frac{16}{25}" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383282 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536094 true] [17592186383282 1111 #uuid "69574a77-66da-5d9a-8b71-a654a9d4e77a" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383283 1034 "1" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383283 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536094 true] [17592186383283 1111 #uuid "aed7529e-d700-58d5-a5f1-a1c93190507a" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383284 1034 "\\text{DNE}" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383284 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536094 true] [17592186383284 1111 #uuid "96927685-6a85-5698-97cf-0f275157c475" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383285 1034 "0" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383285 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536094 true] [17592186383285 1111 #uuid "db598533-959e-5159-871c-46bd87099160" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383286 1017 #edb/ref 17592186383287 13194139536094 true] [17592186383286 1089 "q-105426" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383286 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536094 true] [17592186383286 1100 "${lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\theta \\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }=$" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383286 1113 #uuid "2b7f6b18-e042-5b37-92b3-e2e8dfeb7c5a" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383286 1145 "First, we can simplify the limit using trigonometric identities, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\theta \\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta } & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }÷\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }÷\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }\\cdot {lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate the limits separately:\n\n- Consider the first limit. Notice that as $\\theta \\to 0,$ both numerator and denominator approach $0.$ \n\nSo, if we attempt to evaluate the limit directly, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{0}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is an indeterminate form. \n\nInstead, let's recall the following special limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Consider the second limit. Evaluating it directly, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡0=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }\\cdot {lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =1\\cdot 1=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383287 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383288 13194139536094 true] [17592186383287 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383289 13194139536094 true] [17592186383287 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383290 13194139536094 true] [17592186383287 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383291 13194139536094 true] [17592186383287 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383292 13194139536094 true] [17592186383287 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536094 true] [17592186383287 1041 "selection" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383287 1104 #edb/ref 17592186383289 13194139536094 true] [17592186383287 1110 #uuid "5821d289-1a70-5ffa-8441-7239ffaf2a26" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383288 1034 "2" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383288 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536094 true] [17592186383288 1111 #uuid "244629a0-6b61-5a65-ae36-fab6860a5bd4" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383289 1034 "1" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383289 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536094 true] [17592186383289 1111 #uuid "8e30c4e8-9983-5693-bc89-04abe639d17b" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383290 1034 "\\text{DNE}" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383290 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536094 true] [17592186383290 1111 #uuid "cd41cdea-3221-599c-816f-1730ff0d4382" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383291 1034 "0" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383291 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536094 true] [17592186383291 1111 #uuid "5df462f7-abb7-5dc4-8d72-4c2716c99efa" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383292 1034 "-1" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383292 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536094 true] [17592186383292 1111 #uuid "acc2c55a-e18d-52ac-bdf0-b333b7fddc5f" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383293 1017 #edb/ref 17592186383294 13194139536094 true] [17592186383293 1089 "q-302827" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383293 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536094 true] [17592186383293 1100 "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383293 1113 #uuid "2c2bb74d-654b-5f71-a360-a61566e9b5c7" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383293 1145 "First, we can simplify the limit using trigonometric identities, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }{\\theta } & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }}{\\theta } \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }\\cdot {lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate the limits separately:\n\n- Consider the first limit. Notice that as $\\theta \\to 0,$ both numerator and denominator approach $0.$ \n\nSo, if we attempt to evaluate the limit directly, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }=\\frac{0}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is an indeterminate form. \n\nInstead, let's recall the following special limit:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }=1\n$$\n\n- Consider the second limit. Evaluating it directly, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡0}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }\\cdot {lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta } & =1\\cdot 1=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }=1.\n$$" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383294 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383295 13194139536094 true] [17592186383294 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536094 true] [17592186383294 1041 "field-1" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383294 1104 #edb/ref 17592186383295 13194139536094 true] [17592186383294 1110 #uuid "1a3d43fd-1060-51c4-8c36-841ed8cb0237" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383295 1034 "1" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383295 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536094 true] [17592186383295 1111 #uuid "68966577-c1d3-5fa0-bd79-53a39e4dfe9c" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383296 1017 #edb/ref 17592186383297 13194139536094 true] [17592186383296 1089 "q-339692" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383296 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536094 true] [17592186383296 1100 "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,(-\\frac{21\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{4x})=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383296 1113 #uuid "465664e9-9e79-5042-b31f-cc26731fd988" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383296 1145 "Notice that as $x\\to 0,$ both numerator and denominator approach $0.$\n\nSo, if we attempt to evaluate the limit directly, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{21\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{4x}=\\frac{0}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is an indeterminate form.\n\nInstead, let's recall the following special limit:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}=1\n$$\n\nRewriting the given limit using the algebra of limits and applying our special limit, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,(\\frac{21\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{4x}) & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}(-\\frac{21}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{21}{4}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{21}{4}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{21}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383297 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383298 13194139536094 true] [17592186383297 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383299 13194139536094 true] [17592186383297 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536094 true] [17592186383297 1041 "field-1" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383297 1104 #edb/ref 17592186383298 13194139536094 true] [17592186383297 1110 #uuid "76937d7a-eb36-5682-9b24-95f020347fbb" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383298 1034 "-\\frac{21}{4}" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383298 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536094 true] [17592186383298 1111 #uuid "ba51663a-cf49-5ab7-996a-75a703853cf1" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383299 1034 "0" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383299 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536094 true] [17592186383299 1111 #uuid "261e6f16-3b2e-587e-8d2d-fe99babfa8e3" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383300 1017 #edb/ref 17592186383301 13194139536094 true] [17592186383300 1089 "q-339798" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383300 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536094 true] [17592186383300 1100 "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{sin}^{5}⁡x}{4{x}^{4}}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383300 1113 #uuid "a6d95c69-caf3-511b-b6ef-078487caf544" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383300 1145 "Notice that as $x\\to 0,$ both numerator and denominator approach $0.$\n\nSo, if we attempt to evaluate the limit directly, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{{sin}^{5}⁡x}{4{x}^{4}}=\\frac{0}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is an indeterminate form.\n\nInstead, let's recall the following special limit:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}=1\n$$\n\nRewriting the given limit using the algebra of limits and applying our special limit, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{{sin}^{5}⁡x}{4{x}^{4}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}(\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{{sin}^{4}⁡x}{{x}^{4}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{{sin}^{4}⁡x}{{x}^{4}}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to 0}{(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x})}^{4}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {[{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}]}^{4}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {1}^{4}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383301 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383302 13194139536094 true] [17592186383301 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536094 true] [17592186383301 1041 "field-1" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383301 1104 #edb/ref 17592186383302 13194139536094 true] [17592186383301 1110 #uuid "16eb4281-0d49-524b-95c0-084d48c5bcf7" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383302 1034 "0" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383302 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536094 true] [17592186383302 1111 #uuid "48e6d24c-8440-5a91-8411-d737966f2f71" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383303 1017 #edb/ref 17592186383304 13194139536094 true] [17592186383303 1089 "q-340137" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383303 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536094 true] [17592186383303 1100 "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1}{3\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383303 1113 #uuid "c70f0c51-11a4-5b22-b4c6-7f265fa6778d" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383303 1145 "First, we can simplify the limit using trigonometric identities, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1}{3\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }{3\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{(\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta })}{3\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{1}{3\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{1}{3{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta }) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }\\cdot {lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{1}{3{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate the limits separately:\n\n- Consider the first limit. Notice that as $\\theta \\to 0,$ both numerator and denominator approach $0.$ \n\nSo, if we attempt to evaluate the limit directly, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }=\\frac{0}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is an indeterminate form. \n\nInstead, let's recall the following special limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta } & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Consider the second limit. Evaluating it directly, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{1}{3{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{1}{3{cos}^{4}⁡0}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta })\\cdot {lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{1}{3{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta } & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383304 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383305 13194139536094 true] [17592186383304 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536094 true] [17592186383304 1041 "field-1" 13194139536094 true] [17592186383304 1104 #edb/ref 17592186383305 13194139536094 true] [17592186383304 1110 #uuid "bcf945d2-2c69-587d-